uestion/id #uuid "d99d7426-520b-5e1d-945d-430bc4355051" :question/math-academy-id "q-130510" :question/problem "Represent the following system of equations using matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-1 &=4y \\\\ y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y &=1 \\\\ 0x+y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265924 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6149c1e3-2adb-5ef4-9f00-d3b2f8ea2b11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263840} {:answer/id #uuid "ae8b8a48-bedd-5065-93e5-a6639b2ed96c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264503} {:answer/id #uuid "b1b9dd15-da63-5ed4-bc90-f1be32942872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264529} {:answer/id #uuid "b5a71f49-1f77-5bf1-a994-f837b58aa69