ld/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299443}] :question/id #uuid "a86d8468-1029-529b-a5d8-f3aa18370d7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-317521" :question/problem "For the following system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+5 &=y \\\\ 3x-2y &=7,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nits representation using matrices is\n\n| |  | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $x$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $y$ |  | | $=$ | |  | {{field-4}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $7$ |  | |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-1}} | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." :question/worked-solution "First, we organize the system so that it is in the correct order and  both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=-5 \\\\ 3x-2y &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299617 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ecd663bb-16f1-5a4a-97e3-d46851159337" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298560} :answer-field/id #uuid "36ce1f5a-b325-52e2-9f07-3f178f4d5d1