/problem "If $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $B,$ which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $Bx=0$ has only zero solution\n- **II.** $\\text{Col}(B)\\ne {R}^{2}$\n- **III.** $\\text{nullity}(B)=0$" :question/worked-solution "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix $M,$ we have the following by the invertible matrix theorem:\n\n$M$ is invertible $\\,⇔\\,{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(M)={R}^{2} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(M))=2=\\text{rank}(M) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(M)={0} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(M))=0=\\text{nullity}(M)\\end{aligned}$\n\nLet's now apply the theorem to the matrix $M=B-0I=B.$\n\n- Statement I is false. Notice that if $\\lambda =0$ is an eigenvalue of $B,$ then the nonzero solutions of $(B-0I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $B.$ As a result, the matrix $M=B$ must be singular.\n\n- Statement II is true. Since $M=B$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{Col}(B)\\ne {R}^{2}.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $M=B$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that \n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(B)\\ne 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362248 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "319126a6-cb98-5c29-8c30-bfd20133ec43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452443} {:answer/id #uuid "285ae59e-5ddd-5dc9-862d-3bc834ee97db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452444} :answer-field/id #uuid "cff45205-5a50-56b9-95a8-9585e7c8f98c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453069} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "632c7bfe-66b2-5e98-9e93-398f5b32a709" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answ