(A+I)x=0$ are eigenvectors of $A.$ As a result, the matrix $M=A+I$ must be singular.\n\n- Statements II and III are false. Since $M=A+I$ is singular, by the invertible matrix theorem, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A+I)\\ne 3,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\text{Null}(A+I)\\ne {0}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362249 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6786d395-a50b-5882-ae31-36863216b6c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452449} {:answer/id #uuid "724b23f9-2a73-506f-899d-a1e9be5b76dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452450}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452450} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e20e3ee-4bcc-5a2e-9b67-c327aaad4254" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453072} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2209fa5-8e22-578c-b332-194b1ee18867" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452451} {:answer/id #uuid "558318e4-8fd5-5b1a-836d-4e23c5796f09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452451} :answer-field/id #uuid "5bbe6d9a-5be5-5570-b069-1d4b26576b7f" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186453073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bb34267-89b0-514a-80f5-0d7551327ba7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452453} {:answer/id #uuid "d47f5619-55b0-58a2-956d-cdc273e67787" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186452454}] :answer-field/correct {:ans