ute ${W}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{4} & ={W}^{2}\\cdot {W}^{2} \\\\  & =W\\cdot W \\\\  & ={W}^{2} \\\\  & =W\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{W}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186375916 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3033aa1-cb1b-51d7-bd66-84b07ac416e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375918} {:answer/id #uuid "0864e58a-33de-52c4-a01e-09b896904513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375919} {:answer/id #uuid "38d0d5d6-e7f8-51b0-a5c1-d9f6154b91c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375920} {:answer/id #uuid "27092bc7-551b-5545-b710-7b71ed7f703f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375921} {:answer/id #uuid "b642da4d-bd4e-52d0-9efc-082398abd7df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375919} :answer-field/id #uuid "730549d1-5dd7-5d03-a4f9-dc98698c3514" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186375917}] :question/id #uuid "5b7ea406-9f82-5933-b31e-095d9f01e027" :question/math-academy-id "q-130646" :question/problem "If $C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${C}^{4}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${C}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{2} & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${C}^{2}=C,$ so $C$ is an idempotent matrix.  \n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${C}^{4}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}^{4} & ={C}^{2}\\cdot {C}^{2} \\\\  & =C\\cdot C \\\\  & ={C}^{2} \\\\  & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{C}^{4}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186377735 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f1ec707-d108-5c5f-95b9-f01b95149735" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377737} {:answer/id #uuid "3ceb5c0a-088d-5afe-9529-7e677309be1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377738} {:answer/id #uuid "16377926-6078-5e5e-8a56-d2bb1659e827" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377739} {:answer/id #uuid "1d542b8a-f667-583d-8708-e581bf10d752" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377740} {:answer/id #uuid "558c0201-332f-5cb3-b439-ba474404267a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377741}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377740} :answer-field/id #uuid "d57be3b3-e112-57f7-b6a6-16bbac625c72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186377736}] :question/id #uuid "07ba9ea7-a44e-52e4-bff2-32246bba4f40" :question/math-academy-id "q-78576" :question/problem "If $U=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${U}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${U}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{2} & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${U}^{2}=U,$ so $U$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${U}^{3}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{3} & ={U}^{2}\\cdot U \\\\  & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & ={U}^{2} \\\\  & =U\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{U}^{3}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186379372 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "486cf915-4729-5348-a631-1139c564eaa9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379374} {:answer/id #uuid "7e9c83be-9f24-5f3f-a844-8cd7595ce2a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379375} {:answer/id #uuid "a2b76ef5-d10d-55c7-a887-ad88a55019ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186379376} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f49551-908e-5122-852e-5f3eff7e718e" :answer/typ