id "q-78574" :question/problem "If \n$P=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}$, then ${P}^{6}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, we compute ${P}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{2} & =P\\cdot P \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that ${P}^{2}=P,$ so $P$ is an idempotent matrix.\n\nWe can use this fact to compute ${P}^{6}$ quickly, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{6} & ={P}^{2}\\cdot {P}^{2}\\cdot {P}^{2} \\\\  & =P\\cdot P\\cdot P \\\\  & ={P}^{2}\\cdot P \\\\  & =P\\cdot P \\\\  & ={P}^{2} \\\\  & =P\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{P}^{6}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186390750 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51ba5d1d-917f-578b-b236-84c5ce425052" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390752} {:answer/id #uuid "9dbe959f-5587-55cc-8bae-e699339e8f4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390753} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7a779e-0566-5402-a151-8dcb0f8c03e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186390754} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea01b22-3015-5978-9cd8-0f6cd3a74b94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{